From 943959cad55bb3245e62fe703d636d3d328f3b3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:10:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Wallet lock: lock only the wallet files the Swarm audits
 reviewed (owner clarification)

The owner asked for the lock to cover only what would invalidate a wallet audit. scripts/wallet-lock.mjs now names an
explicit list instead of name patterns: the wallet sign-in files of the R5-R12 audits and the wallet controller, GOLD
purchase, checkouts, staking panel, balances, server GOLD/recovery code, deploy tool and their tests of Submission13-18
(audits e4a57f91 .. f6bd50ad), plus the lock itself: 70 files, all identical to 7021b5b (Worker a92a767c). Files no
wallet audit reviewed, styles, worker/app.ts and wrangler.jsonc are free to change. The lock is a warning, not a ban:
with the owner's approval the hashes are refreshed with a reason and the change deploys as usual, then needs a new
Swarm audit. Full suite 3640 tests, 0 fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
