 # Wallet lock (錢包封鎖區)
 
-The wallet, sign-in and payment code passed the Swarm audits (last one `f6bd50ad`, fixed in `7021b5b`, Worker `a92a767c`).
-It is frozen: `security/wallet-lock.json` holds the hash of every file in the zone (`ZONE` in `scripts/wallet-lock.mjs`),
-and `tests/wallet-lock.test.mjs` fails if any of them changes, is removed, or a new file appears in the zone. The deploy
-tool runs the full suite, so such a change cannot be deployed by accident. The lock is a warning, not a ban: once the owner
-approves, the change can be made and deployed as usual (re-audit timing is the owner's call).
+The wallet-related files that the Swarm audits reviewed (wallet sign-in R5-R12; wallet controller, GOLD purchase,
+checkouts, staking panel and deploy tool in Submission13-18, last audit `f6bd50ad`, fixed in `7021b5b`, Worker `a92a767c`)
+are locked: `LOCKED` in `scripts/wallet-lock.mjs`, hashes in `security/wallet-lock.json`. `tests/wallet-lock.test.mjs` fails
+if one of them changes or is removed, and the deploy tool runs the full suite, so such a change cannot be deployed by
+accident. Changing a locked file means the audit no longer covers what runs.
 
-- Do not edit files in the zone. If a task seems to need it, stop and warn the owner first, in plain Chinese, that the
-  change will need a new Swarm audit (「這會動到錢包封鎖區，改完必須重新送 Swarm audit」), and wait for their decision. The owner
-  considers this very important.
-- The same warning applies to changes outside the zone that alter wallet or payment behaviour: the payment routes in
-  `worker/app.ts`, shared helpers the zone imports, the `/api/gold`, `/api/economy` and `/api/celestao-checkout` settings in
-  `wrangler.jsonc`, contract addresses and prices.
-- Only after the owner explicitly approves: make the change, then
-  `node scripts/wallet-lock.mjs --update --reason "what changed and who approved it"`, and tell the owner a re-audit is due.
+The lock is a warning, not a ban:
+- Before editing a locked file, warn the owner in plain Chinese (「這會動到錢包封鎖區，改完必須重新送 Swarm audit」) and wait
+  for their decision. The owner considers this very important.
+- Once they approve: make the change, run `node scripts/wallet-lock.mjs --update --reason "what changed and who approved it"`,
+  and deploy as usual. Remind them the change needs a new Swarm audit; when to send it is their call.
+- Give the same warning for a change outside the lock that alters how a locked file behaves (for example the GOLD and
+  checkout routes in `worker/app.ts`, or their settings in `wrangler.jsonc`).
 - Never refresh the hashes just to make the test pass, and never weaken or skip `tests/wallet-lock.test.mjs`.
-- `node scripts/wallet-lock.mjs` alone checks the zone.
+- `node scripts/wallet-lock.mjs` alone checks the lock.
